# Gwenda colors

For any question about brand colors, backgrounds, hex values, or Canva swatches:

1. Read **`docs/colors.md`** first (or `src/config/colors.json` for machine values).
2. Answer with the **exact hex** from that doc. Do not guess or approximate.
3. Do not invent warmer charcoal substitutes (e.g. `#1c1b18`) unless the user asks to change the palette.

## Solid swatches (memorize these)

| Name | Hex |
|------|-----|
| Background | `#0d0d0d` |
| Background elevated | `#141414` |
| Background story | `#151414` |
| Background story print | `#23211b` |
| Background card | `#1a1a1a` |
| Text | `#e8e4dc` |
| Text muted | `#8a8680` |
| Gold | `#c9a84c` |
| Error | `#c97a7a` |

Default page background is **`#0d0d0d`**, not `#141414`.

For story section off-site (Canva, print): use **`#23211b`** (`bgStoryPrint`). Do not use `#141414` or `#151414` — too dark and cold for flat fills.
